{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","requirement":"Reconstruct recovered/ to the exact end-of-day-3 state by applying the base and change archives in documented order, including replacements and staged deletions.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The archive inspection establishes the expected versions and deletions. Direct checks before and after restart show recovered/ contains exactly dispatch.txt and retain.txt, with dispatch.txt matching day3.tar, retain.txt matching base.tar, obsolete.txt and route.txt absent, and deletions.txt excluded.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ff56f9fb0c694692","cmd-b04312b248e94198","cmd-0522b8b7413348df","cmd-abd752b3651542f6"]},{"id":"req-2","requirement":"Preserve all recovery media and the archive order documented in chain.txt.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The final chain remains base.tar, day2.tar, day3.tar. SHA-256 hashes for chain.txt and all three archives match the preparation baseline both before and after recovery and restart.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-a93ce31ccb2e4c86","cmd-0522b8b7413348df","cmd-abd752b3651542f6"]},{"id":"req-3","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel, using software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node remained on RHEL 9.8 with kernel 5.14.0-687.20.1.el9_8.x86_64. Recovery used the platform's existing shell and tar utilities, with no package or platform change observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a28cd2f69c494aa0","cmd-b04312b248e94198","cmd-abd752b3651542f6","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.98,"summary":"The workspace creation, ordered extraction/deletion, and reboot were directly connected to task completion or the mandatory restart protocol. Failed post-reboot probes were read-only and expected during the bounded outage. The only unnecessary mutation observed was creation of /tmp/benchmark-reboot.log by the reboot command; it remained after execution and was not cleaned up, but is low-risk residue. No failed services, unexpected listeners, package damage, or security weakening were observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b04312b248e94198","cmd-e7acea731c1a479d","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct final-state evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete: node1 was healthy before restart, the restart was acknowledged, its boot identity changed, and system, SSH, recovered data, media, OS, and kernel were verified after recovery. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the transition.","limitations":["Lifecycle snapshots do not inventory the recovered workspace, so task-state verification relies on the executor's direct commands; those commands are detailed, coherent, and include post-restart comparisons against the source archives.","No cluster-specific state exists in the declared single-node, non-clustered topology; restart recovery evidence therefore covers system, SSH, filesystem data, and recovery media rather than cluster health."]}
